doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20820859"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - remaining useful life
  - predictive maintenance
  - NASA CMAPSS
  - prognostics and health management
  - model evaluation
  - explanation faithfulness
abstract: >-
  Code, inference traces and analysis for a four-part protocol for evaluating
  large language models on remaining useful life prediction: no-skill baselines,
  rank correlation, output entropy, and a faithfulness test for the generated
  explanations. Five open-weight model configurations were evaluated on FD001,
  including Llama 3.1 8B at two quantisation levels, with the reference model run
  on all four CMAPSS sub-datasets. The release holds the complete corpus of 5,557
  model responses, a manifest with per-run checksums and recomputed metrics, and
  the scripts that generate every table and figure in the paper.
